
  <sn><md>### Understanding the rclone Sync Mechanism

`rclone sync` makes the **destination an exact copy of the source**.

**Basic Mechanism**

```text
SOURCE  ───────►  DESTINATION
   A                 B
```

When you run:

```bash
rclone sync SOURCE DESTINATION
```

rclone compares both locations and performs the necessary actions.

| Situation                                 | What rclone does                |
| ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| File exists in source but not destination | Copies it to destination     |
| File changed in source                    | Updates the destination file |
| File is identical                         | Skips it                     |
| File exists only in destination           | Deletes it from destination |
| Folder becomes empty                      | May remove it               |
</md></sn>
